<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
<title>{{ site_config.short_title|default("Stablecoin Blacklisting") }} — Overview</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Serif+4:opsz,wght@8..60,400;8..60,500;8..60,600&family=Inter+Tight:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/dashboard.css" />
</head>
<body class="dark">

<header class="header">
  <div class="header-top">
    <div class="theme-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Theme" style="margin-left:auto">
      <button data-theme="light" title="Light">☀</button>
      <button data-theme="dark" class="active" title="Dark">☾</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h1>When does compliance become <em>censorship</em>?</h1>
  <p class="subhead">A stablecoin freeze is a mechanism where centralized issuers, like Tether (USDT) or Circle (USDC), use smart contract code to block specific addresses from moving their stablecoins. Every freeze stablecoin issuers have executed can be traced. This dashboard maps on‑chain action to the legal or regulatory event behind it. Hover the timeline to read each cluster; drag the band below to zoom into a window.</p>
  <nav class="nav">
    <a href="index.html" class="current">Overview</a>
    <a href="explore.html">Explore</a>
    <a href="entities.html">Entities</a>
    <a href="sources.html">Sources</a>
    {% if has_notes %}<a href="notes.html">Notes</a>{% endif %}
    <a href="methodology.html">Methodology</a>
  </nav>
</header>

<section class="kpis" id="kpi-strip">
  <!-- KPIs render here -->
</section>

<section class="controls" id="controls">
  <div class="filter-group" data-filter="category">
    <button class="chip showing-btn" id="showing-btn" aria-pressed="true" title="Toggle all categories">All</button>
    <button class="chip" data-value="ofac" aria-pressed="true"><span class="chip-dot" style="background:var(--bl)"></span>OFAC <span class="chip-count">—</span></button>
    <button class="chip" data-value="court" aria-pressed="true"><span class="chip-dot" style="background:var(--court)"></span>Court <span class="chip-count">—</span></button>
    <button class="chip" data-value="hack" aria-pressed="true"><span class="chip-dot" style="background:var(--hack)"></span>Hack <span class="chip-count">—</span></button>
    <button class="chip" data-value="untriggered" aria-pressed="true"><span class="chip-dot" style="background:var(--na);border:2px solid var(--na);box-sizing:border-box"></span>No public reason <span class="chip-count">—</span></button>
  </div>
  <button class="reset" id="reset-btn">↺ Reset view</button>
</section>

<section class="main">
  <div class="main-left">
    <div class="chart-wrap">
      <svg class="timeline-svg" id="timeline" viewBox="0 0 1600 460" preserveAspectRatio="none"></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="brush-wrap">
      <svg class="brush-svg" id="brush" viewBox="0 0 1600 64" preserveAspectRatio="none"></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="detail-card empty" id="detail">
      <div class="dc-head">
        <span class="dc-date">—</span>
        <span class="dc-tag muted">SELECT A BUBBLE</span>
      </div>
      <div class="dc-body"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <aside class="main-right">
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
        <h3>Reason mix</h3>
        <p>Clusters in current view, by attributed cause</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel-body">
        <div class="donut-wrap">
          <svg class="donut-svg" id="donut" viewBox="0 0 100 100"></svg>
          <div class="donut-list" id="donut-list"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
        <h3>Largest events</h3>
        <p>Biggest single‑day clusters in view</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel-body">
        <div class="top-list" id="top-list"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel year">
      <div class="panel-head">
        <h3>By year</h3>
        <p>Wallets affected · stacked by reason</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel-body">
        <div class="year-bars" id="year-bars"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </aside>
</section>

<footer class="footer">
  <div class="footer-grid">
    <div>
      <h4>About this dataset</h4>
      <p>We track every <code>BLACKLIST</code> and <code>UNBLACKLIST</code> transaction emitted by Circle's USDC contracts on Ethereum and five other EVM chains, then attempt to attribute each to a public trigger — an OFAC SDN action, a court order, an exchange hack response, or otherwise. Where we cannot find one, the action is recorded but flagged as <em>no public reason</em>.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4>Method</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="methodology.html">Methodology</a></li>
        <li><a href="sources.html">Sources cited</a></li>
        {% if site_config.github_repo_url %}<li><a href="{{ site_config.github_repo_url }}">Source repository</a></li>{% endif %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4>Cite</h4>
      <p>{{ site_config.authors|default("Lee") }}, <em>{{ site_config.dataset_title|default("Stablecoin Blacklisting") }}</em>, {{ site_config.citation_period|default("May 2026") }}.<br/><span id="last-updated" style="color:var(--ink-soft)">Last Updated: …</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

<div class="tooltip" id="tooltip"></div>

<script src="assets/dashboard.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
